# keiro-dsl writes a paste-ready Cabal fragment beside the generated layer on
# every scaffold. It is an instruction to a human, not a build input: its blocks
# are pasted into shikigami-core.cabal, which is what the build reads. The
# scaffold ledger and the conformance ledger beside it ARE committed -- they are
# the machine-owned history the next scaffold reads to report stale paths.
shikigami-core/src/keiro-dsl-cabal-fragment.workspace.*.txt

# keiro-dsl check/coverage/diff reports (`just keiro-check`, `just keiro-diff`).
build/

# Immutable generated-edition migration backups stay local.
shikigami-core/src/.keiro-dsl-generated-haskell-migrations/
